{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical layer physical layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","fileName":"Physical Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical layer physical layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","fileName":"Physical Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Physical Layer","heading":"Physical Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The physical layer carries raw bits as electrical, optical, or radio signals over a medium. It concerns the mechanics and signaling needed for a device to place bits on a channel and receive them from that channel.\n\nHigher layers can describe frames, addresses, and protocols only after this layer supplies an actual transmission path. Signal strength and the characteristics of the medium can therefore affect integrity and throughput above it.","tags":["baby"],"links":["OSI Layers Packets and Network Streams","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"physical layer physical layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Physical Layer.md","fileName":"Physical Layer.m